I found three instances of the target symbol, all in the foyer area. They are the square-with-crosshair symbols that have a ">" chevron inside the circle.

Other square-with-crosshair symbols in the drawing look similar but have a diagonal line or X inside the circle instead, so I did not count them. I checked these in zoomed views of the kitchen, living room, stairs, hall and both bedroom areas. I did not zoom in on the bathrooms, garage or porch, so any instance there would be missed.

{"count": 3, "shapes": [{"cx": 957, "cy": 745}, {"cx": 957, "cy": 912}, {"cx": 957, "cy": 1077}]}

I counted 7 instances without zooming, so none were checked at high resolution. The reference is a tall, narrow fixture with a circle and about 60% of its length filled black. I matched it to the short standalone fixtures that have a black portion with the circle at the boundary, some rotated.

I left out the black segments inside the long strips, such as those along x=101 and x=307, because they look like separate longer fixtures rather than this symbol. If those are meant to count, the total would be higher.

