I found two instances of the symbol, both on the curved counter in the lower middle of the drawing. They are at about (474, 766) and (483, 885).

I left out a similar-looking circle at about (1041, 269). It has a plain cross inside the circle rather than the hash (#) pattern in the reference. This one is a judgement call, and it would make the count 3 if it does match.

{"count": 2, "shapes": [{"cx": 474, "cy": 766}, {"cx": 483, "cy": 885}]}

I found four instances of the BE symbol, all identified from the overview without zooming. They are at (433,70), (319,452), (492,838) and (432,1207).

I excluded the WM symbols, the B symbols (including the one at (575,1210)) and the GE symbol at (137,1310), because they look different from the BE reference.

{"count": 4, "shapes": [{"cx": 433, "cy": 70}, {"cx": 319, "cy": 452}, {"cx": 492, "cy": 838}, {"cx": 432, "cy": 1208}]}

I count 6 instances of the target symbol. The target is a plain circle with a vertical line through it. I excluded circles with a horizontal bar through them, such as the GWP receptacles. I also excluded the circles marked J and F1.

Two calls were uncertain. The circle at (596, 967) is next to an "AG" label, and I counted it because it looked plain at zoom. The circles at (575, 522) and (577, 569) looked hatched, so I left them out.

